# Copy to .env for local runs:  cp .env.example .env
# Then:  export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit real values.
#
# In GitHub Actions these come from repository secrets instead
# (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions), not from this file.
# The names below are exactly what .github/workflows/evening.yml passes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED — the pipeline cannot complete without all five
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Market data + the tradable universe (https://alpaca.markets -> Home -> API Keys).
# Paper-trading keys are sufficient and are what you should use: nothing in this
# project places orders, so a live key grants access it does not need.
# NOTE: a free/Basic Alpaca plan serves IEX data only, which reports a small
# fraction of consolidated volume. The scanner's volume thresholds are not yet
# calibrated for that — see the audit before trusting a run.
ALPACA_API_KEY=
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY=

# Claude scoring (https://console.anthropic.com -> API Keys). Needs billing enabled.
# Read implicitly by anthropic.Anthropic() in src/scorer.py.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Email delivery (https://resend.com/api-keys).
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Recipient(s). Comma-separated for multiple.
EMAIL_TO=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — sensible defaults in code; set only to override
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Sender address. Defaults to onboarding@resend.dev, which Resend only permits
# to deliver to the account owner's own address — set a verified-domain sender
# before mailing anyone else.
# RESEND_FROM=alerts@yourdomain.com

# Scoring model. Defaults to claude-sonnet-4-6.
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A trap worth knowing about
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALPACA_API_KEY and ALPACA_SECRET_KEY are read with a "" fallback
# (src/scanner.py:46-47), so leaving them blank does NOT fail at startup — it
# fails later with an opaque authentication error, after the run has already
# started. EMAIL_TO and RESEND_API_KEY are read at the very END of the run
# (src/emailer.py:107,112), so a missing value there wastes the entire scan and
# every Claude call before it raises. Fill all five in before running.
